WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.221
Open Deployments in Omni IC and choose Open.

00:00:03.401 --> 00:00:07.583
Find the training deployment by name and check its
status and date range.

00:00:07.763 --> 00:00:13.501
Here, Community Support is Demobilizing, so this is a
good time to review the crew's paperwork.

00:00:13.821 --> 00:00:16.936
On the deployment, check the date and the selected
crew.

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.719
A missing report applies to that crew and date.

00:00:19.899 --> 00:00:26.085
You can start a report where your permissions allow
it, or change the date to review one that already
exists.

00:00:26.405 --> 00:00:30.501
Open the Date picker and select November second for
this exercise.

00:00:30.681 --> 00:00:35.289
The date is part of the report's scope, so confirm it
before reviewing the hours.

00:00:35.609 --> 00:00:37.359
Choose Done to apply the date.

00:00:37.539 --> 00:00:41.891
The crew is the same, but the report list now shows
the entries for that day.

00:00:42.211 --> 00:00:46.435
This crew report is marked Approved and totals eleven
and a half hours.

00:00:46.615 --> 00:00:49.708
Compare the date, crew, total, and status together.

00:00:49.888 --> 00:00:54.048
That helps you avoid treating a draft for another day
as the approved record.

00:00:54.368 --> 00:00:56.416
The next day's report is a draft.

00:00:56.596 --> 00:01:01.481
In the note field for the intended entry, write a
short note that explains the change.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:04.093
Here we note a fictional rehearsal check-in.

00:01:04.273 --> 00:01:10.929
A wildland contractor or an industrial response team
can use this same field to explain a crew entry.

00:01:11.249 --> 00:01:14.279
Choose Save entries to keep the change in the draft.

00:01:14.459 --> 00:01:16.656
Submit report is a separate action.

00:01:16.836 --> 00:01:21.252
Leave the draft available for review until the
required checks are complete.

00:01:21.572 --> 00:01:24.175
The screen confirms that the entries were saved.

00:01:24.355 --> 00:01:26.104
The report still says Draft.

00:01:26.284 --> 00:01:32.236
That gives the next reviewer the updated details and
a clear indication that approval has not happened.

00:01:32.556 --> 00:01:36.097
Reopen the report and look for the note on the same
crew entry.

00:01:36.277 --> 00:01:45.451
This final check is useful whenever work changes
hands, from a search team demobilizing to a community
response team closing out a standby.
